+# LightCraft ChatGPT connection
+
+This local modification adds an optional native ChatGPT connection to the Windows desktop app.
+Other platforms retain their original editor and explicitly report unsupported auth commands.
+Open **ChatGPT connection…** at the bottom right, then **Continue with ChatGPT**.
+The browser asks you to authorize this app independently of the other Craft apps.
+Account connection is implemented; AI editing and inference are not part of this change.
+
+## Protocol and storage
+
+- Official dynamic registration, a stable app-specific UUID host, loopback callback,
+  PKCE S256, state/nonce checks, and verified RS256/ES256 OpenAI ID tokens.
+- Issued client IDs are retained before code exchange. Reauthorization is bound to
+  the selected client and verified identity. Disconnect removes the registration.
+- Granted scopes determine plan permission. Renewal atomically replaces rotating tokens.
+- Tokens are encrypted with AES-256-GCM; the encryption key lives in the Windows
+  Credential Manager. No plaintext storage fallback. Windows Schannel provides TLS, avoiding a new C/C++ crypto or D-Bus build dependency. Separate app directories.
+- One process owns credential rotation at a time. Callback and HTTPS reads are bounded.
+- Disconnect clears local credentials and attempts remote revocation. If that fails,
+  the app directs you to https://chatgpt.com/settings/usage.
+- The desktop wrapper forwards all editor lifecycle hooks, preferences, autosaves,
+  and native-menu input. Engine/document files and web/WASM targets are untouched.
+- Authentication commands are native platform operations, available headlessly:
+  `lightcraft --chatgpt-status`, `--chatgpt-sign-in`, `--chatgpt-refresh`, and
+  `--chatgpt-disconnect`. Status never returns credentials.
+
+## Validation status (2026-10-06)
+
+Windows Application Control blocks the installed Cargo toolchain (OS error 4551).
+Rust syntax and TOML can be inspected here, but compilation, Rust tests, Clippy,
+visual UI verification, and a real account sign-in remain UNVERIFIED.
+Cargo.lock must be regenerated by an allowed Cargo toolchain before release.
+This checkout is a draft, not a tested installer. No code was pushed or published.
+
+On an authorized build machine, run:
+
+```sh
+cargo fmt --all
+cargo test -p lightcraft chatgpt
+cargo clippy -p lightcraft --all-targets -- -D warnings
+cargo xtask ci
+cargo run -p lightcraft
+```
+
+Tests cover the RFC 7636 PKCE vector, hostile callbacks, returning client binding,
+scope/expiry checks, token-redacted status, signed identity claims, forged ID tokens, and encrypted-data corruption.
+Then test a real sign-in, restart, renewal, cancellation, disconnect, and editor save/quit.
+
+Source contract: https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source/sign-in
+UI guidance: https://developers.openai.com/siwc/ui-ux-guidelines
